ns(p[\"bank_deg\"])\n     T  = Vector((cos(pt)*cos(h), cos(pt)*sin(h), sin(pt)))          # +Forward 3D tangent\n     R0 = Vector((sin(h), -cos(h), 0.0))                             # Horizontal Right\n     U0 = Vector((-sin(pt)*cos(h), -sin(pt)*sin(h), cos(pt)))        # Unbanked slope normal\n     R  = cos(bk)*R0 - sin(bk)*U0                                    # Banked +Right across ribbon\n     U  = sin(bk)*R0 + cos(bk)*U0                                    # Banked surface normal Up\n     ```\n     *CRITICAL DIFFERENCE vs our pre-`#32` draft in `v6_sv_env.py`*:\n     1) In our draft (`v6_sv_env.py` lines 51–71), we had `right = right0 * cos(b_eff) + up0 * sin(b_eff)` (opposite sign on `sin(bk)`!), which would tilt the road in the **OPPOSITE** direction of `@track`'s `racing_z` (`P_race_3d == C_3d - racing_offset_m * R`) and `@anim`'s rig roll! Replacing lines 42–75 of `v6_sv_env.py` with `@track`'s exact `(T, R0, U0, R, U)` formula guarantees `0.000 m` Z-error between the road deck and the car's tires on the `+17.4°` banked bowl!\n     2) Also note on the `+17.4°` right-turn Carousel Bowl (`idx=974`, `bank_deg = +17.4° > 0`, `curv_1pm < 0`): with `R = cos(bk)*R0 - sin(bk)*U0`, `-R` (left / outer edge, `sgn = -1.0`) is the **HIGH raised outer rim** (`(-R).z = +sin(bk)*cos(pt) > 0`), while `+R` (right / inner apex) is the low inner edge! Check `bowl_bm` in `v6_sv_env.py` (around line 552): currently `out_sgn = 1.0 if fb0[\"b_eff\"] > 0 else -1.0` — with `@track`'s formula (`bk > 0` lifts `-R`), the raised outer rim is `out_sgn = -1.0 if bk > 0 else 1.0` (i.e. whichever side has `(fb0[\"right\"] * sgn).z > 0`!). Checking `out_sgn = 1.0 if fb0[\"right\"].z >= 0 else -1.0` automatically puts `V6_BankedBowl_NeonWall` on the raised h